<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    The trait the Overlord armor grants on equip (its ApparelExtension.traitsOnEquip), in the
    Medic Warcasket idiom of an own trait beside VFEP_WarcasketTrait: VFEP's trait blocks
    ManualSkilled and Intellectual, which cover Smithing and Research, and a child apparel extension can only add to what a
    granted trait blocks, never subtract. Docs/Specs/Overlord-Work-Trait.md is the design record.

    Mirrored at startup, do not tune here. WorkProfile.Mirror (Source/1.6/WorkProfile.cs, run
    first in Startup.Run on every play-data load) overwrites this def from VFEP_WarcasketTrait
    as the full mod list leaves it, so "Warcaskets can work!", "can haul!" and Hardworking
    Warcaskets shape the Overlord exactly as they shape a Controller pilot without knowing we
    exist. The contract:
      - disabledWorkTags = VFEP's, with ManualDumb swapped for Cleaning (VFEP's hauling
        exemption is a Harmony postfix keyed on its own def, so a copied ManualDumb would lose
        hauling; ManualDumb covers only Hauling and Cleaning) and every tag an openable work
        type carries removed: ManualSkilled, for Smithing, Crafting and Tailoring, and
        Intellectual, for Research and Anomaly's Dark study.
      - disabledWorkTypes = VFEP's, plus every work type the removed tags covered that is not
        openable (Cooking, Construction, Growing, Mining, PlantCutting), plus each openable one
        the mod settings block. The settings default to the fixed rule: Research open, as
        Core's hacking is Research work and needs the Intellectual tag open; Smithing open, as
        Biotech's mech gestation, subcore encoding and mech repair are Smithing work; Crafting,
        Tailoring and Dark study blocked; and any of them open regardless once VFEP's trait, as
        patched, blocks neither its tags nor the type. Written by the settings' ApplyToDefs on
        every load and settings close.
      - degreeDatas[0]: every public field but the text, degree and commonality copied from
        VFEP's degree, and the TraitExtension's fields copied from VFEP's extension. Both copies
        are full overwrites, nulls included, so the Overlord carries exactly what VFEP's trait
        carries on the running game version: on 1.7, painFactor 0 and RestFallRateFactor 1.3 on
        the degree; on 1.6, painFactor 0 on the extension and no stat factors.
    The values below are the mirror's result from an unpatched VFEP trait on 1.7, so the def
    reads correctly on its own. Every field used exists on 1.6 as
    well.

    The extension omits painFactor on purpose, as VFEP's 1.7 copy does: VEF's TraitExtension
    leaves the float uninitialised and its CalculatePain postfix multiplies pain by any value
    other than 1, so an omitted painFactor is zero pain. The mirror overwrites it from VFEP's
    extension before any pawn exists; the XML value would only ever apply if VFEP's trait had no
    extension at all. apparelExclusiveTrait keeps trait-adding mods and the trait-rolling code
    paths from handing this trait to a pawn outside the suit (VEF's TraitSet.GainTrait prefix
    admits it only while a worn apparel lists it in traitsOnEquip).

    The label is VFEP's own, so the Bio tab names the state as it does for every warcasket pilot.
    The description must hold under every profile a patch mod can leave, so it states the suit's
    intent rather than listing work types. It stays short because the tooltip lists the work
    disables beneath it, and on 1.7 the pain and rest-fall factors too.
  -->
  <TraitDef>
    <defName>OLWC_WarcasketTrait_Overlord</defName>
    <commonality>0</commonality>
    <disabledWorkTags>
      <li>Cleaning</li>
      <li>Animals</li>
      <li>Artistic</li>
      <li>Caring</li>
    </disabledWorkTags>
    <disabledWorkTypes>
      <li>Cooking</li>
      <li>Construction</li>
      <li>Growing</li>
      <li>Mining</li>
      <li>PlantCutting</li>
      <li>Tailoring</li>
      <li>Crafting</li>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Anomaly">DarkStudy</li>
    </disabledWorkTypes>
    <degreeDatas>
      <li>
        <label>warcasket</label>
        <description>{PAWN_nameDef} is entombed in a warcasket. Pain has no effect on {PAWN_objective}, and {PAWN_pronoun} can never go into pain shock or drop unconscious from it.\n\nBuilt for a mechanitor, the suit leaves {PAWN_possessive} arms free for bench work, but it is too bulky for most other labor.</description>
        <painFactor>0</painFactor>
        <statFactors>
          <RestFallRateFactor>1.3</RestFallRateFactor>
        </statFactors>
      </li>
    </degreeDatas>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VEF.Pawns.TraitExtension">
        <apparelExclusiveTrait>true</apparelExclusiveTrait>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </TraitDef>
</Defs>
